What is Quantum Sensor Electronics?
Quantum sensor electronics comprise a family of instruments that translate quantum level interactions into actionable data. Unlike classical sensors that rely on macroscopic physical effects, quantum sensors manipulate individual quantum states, allowing them to detect infinitesimal changes in environmental parameters. This capability is essential for applications ranging from magnetic resonance imaging and gravimetric surveying to inertial navigation and real time health monitoring.
